WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-Looks good, huh?
-Looking sharp.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.367
Yeah, this feels so good, man.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.300
Oh, my gosh.
This is the real deal.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.834
I mean, does it --
-Don't get too attached.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.367
-No, yeah. I won't, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.334
As a kid growing up
and dreaming about this,

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:14.000
does it feel surreal to you
when you hold this,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.667
when you have this belt?

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.767
-Every day, man.
I mean, not even --

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.400
Even just the title,
just life, in general.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.200
You know what I mean?
We're very blessed men, right?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.868
-Yeah, we really are.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.067
And do your kids
understand what you do?

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.000
-They're getting --
I mean, my daughter's 14,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.300
so she's kind of
seen the whole process.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.033
But, you know,
I have two sets of twins.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.267
You know, the babies are 2.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.033
The older boys are 5 now.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.734
So, the babies definitely --

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.100
they have no clue
what's going on.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.267
The big boys are starting
to kind of understand

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.033
that Dad
goes to wrestling shows.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.300
That's what he does.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.100
"You going
to the wrestling show?"

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.167
-They just think you go
watch wrestling shows?

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.100
-I don't know -- I'm not really
sure what they think I do.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.033
Because when they --
the times they've seen me,

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:59.067
I'm just kind of
cutting promos and talking.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.634
So I think they think,
"Dad just talks."

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:04.234
But for a long time,
like, through the pandemic,

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.634
they thought
I worked out for a living.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.734
'Cause, you know, we got the gym
at the house and, you know,

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.834
I try to get in there
and do my thing.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.701
-Absolutely.
-And they kind of got into it,

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.200
as well, to just come in there
and hang out and do --

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.400
act like they're working out.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.400
Grab the 5-pound dumbbells.
-That's awesome.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.767
-But that's what they think is
I just work out for a living.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.133
-It's a family business for you,
really.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.767
-Yep.
-It's been in your family.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.901
Who was the first wrestler
in your family?

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.701
-So it --
I mean, it started with

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.601
the High Chief Peter Maivia.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:35.701
He kind of mentored
my father and my uncle,

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.367
Sika and Afa, The Wild Samoans.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.801
They're a tag team.
-The Wild Samoans, absolutely.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.667
-One of the greatest tag teams
of all time.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.133
Hall of Famers.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:44.834
But it actually started --
they -- they were just fans.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.067
And, you know, they went
to a show back in the day

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.767
in San Francisco
at the Cow Palace.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.934
-Peter Maivia was a huge star
back then in the West Coast

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:55.667
at the time,
back in the territory days.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.501
And he was wrestling
Pat Patterson.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.534
And Pat was beating him up
pretty good,

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.567
and my dad and uncle,
they jumped from the crowd

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.367
and kind of got involved.

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.100
And so Pat knew, he was like,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.367
"We got to get these guys
out of the crowd.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.467
We got to teach them
the business, and that way,

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.367
you know, I don't have to worry
about these guys anymore."

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.834
So, yeah.
-Whoa! That's fantastic.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.868
-It goes all the way back
to the '60s and '70s, yeah.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.968
-And then, when you were a kid,
did you know what's going on?

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.834
Did you just have -- Did you
wrestle in the backyard?

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.067
Did you...?
-Man, we wrestled everywhere.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.467
So, my cousins, the Usos,
who are with me in WWE now,

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.234
we would literally wrestle
in every single room.

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.934
We'd get kicked out.
I mean, when their dad

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:32.133
would come back from the road,
we knew to kind of chill out

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:33.467
and take it outside.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:36.834
But when he was off on the road,
it was a free for all.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.400
You know what I mean?
So we were just doing our thing.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.734
We would wrestle in the pool
for hours at times.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:42.868
So, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.400
-We were putting in work
at a very early age.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.667
-I've seen, you know,
a handful of documentaries,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.467
and it's just fascinating.
And you just see all the gigs

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:54.901
that you have to play to end up
even remotely close to WWE.

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.868
But, I mean, you play
high schools, whatever it is.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:01.033
I mean, you do whatever.
And you'd change names

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:04.334
and concepts of what
your character does and is.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.367
It's a rough road, isn't it?
-Yeah, it's --

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.601
I mean, you know, oftentimes,
I say this is like

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:10.467
the blue-collar
form of entertainment.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:14.534
You know, you got to really
pay your dues and, you know --

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.000
you know, go on this journey,
and it's different for everyone.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.400
You know,
I've been very fortunate.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.901
You know,
I have my family background

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.667
that's guided me along the way.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.133
And obviously,
I've been able to tap into

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.868
a potential that, you know,
I was unable to unlock.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.601
But there's a lot of guys,
you know,

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.601
that we have them currently
in the WWE --

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:34.467
you know, guys like Seth Rollins
that I came up with in WWE --

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.901
that have been journeymen,

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:38.868
that have been all over
the independent scene.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.968
You know, wrestling in armories,
high school gyms, like you said.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.801
Yeah, in front of 200,
you know, max people.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.200
-Max.
Sometimes it's 50 people.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.567
-It's not always beautiful.
So, yeah.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.801
I mean,
WWE is the highest you can get.

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:54.667
And we're very proud of that,
you know, getting to this point.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.400
But it can be rough sometimes.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.667
-They just announced big news
in the wrestling world

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:02.334
that Triple H
is retiring as a wrestler.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:05.300
I was going to ask you, what
does Triple H mean to you?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:09.434
I know you --
-Man, you know,

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:13.267
H was very critical in this
process to guide me along.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:16.234
He was kind of --
Before I met Vince

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:19.868
and built a relationship
with him, it was Triple H.

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:23.367
He was the one that
was down there in developmental

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.968
helping guide talent along.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.734
You know, he's the one
that kind of overlooked it.

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.601
And before --
-Developmental's like --

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.601
-It's like the minor leagues of,
you know, WWE.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.901
And before -- now it's NXT.

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.400
And that's
a big platform for us.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.968
You know, they're on Tuesday
nights on USA Network.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:41.067
And they're a big show
themselves now, but before that,

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:44.667
it was just called FCW,
Florida Championship Wrestling,

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.100
in a tiny little warehouse.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.367
And we're wrestling in --
it was like those armories

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:52.567
and the high school gyms,
in front of 50 people.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:53.868
Killing each other for,
you know,

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.300
what felt like nothing
at the time.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:05:00.667
But, yeah, Triple H was huge
in guiding me along.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.968
-He had faith in you?
He was like,

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.334
"I know this kid's
gonna do something"?

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.701
-I think so. Yeah, I think
he recognized the potential.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.601
And he was just
always good to me.

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:09.934
Early on, I was always the type,

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.901
you know,
that was asking for raises.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.467
I was like,
"Can I get some more money?"

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:14.868
And they're like,
"Yeah, go ahead."

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.267
And then, two months later,
"Can I get some more money?"

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.801
"Yep."
And then there was a point

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.801
where they're like, "No."

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.734
And then I was like,
"Well, can you ask Triple H?"

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:26.167
And then, the next morning,
"You're getting more money."

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.567
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:30.200
So, man, H has hooked me up.
He's always looked over me.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.734
He's --
-Don't forget that.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:34.167
-Inside and out, out the ring,
he's the best.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.934
-Yeah, I love always --
any time I've had him

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.167
on the show
or dealt with him, that guy,

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.701
he's a truly genuine,
awesome, great guy.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:42.000
-First class.
-Yeah, this is this Saturday.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.467
"Wrestlemania 38."

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.234
Is it 38 already?
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:46.400
-I know, man.
-That's a big deal.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.000
It is -- This is --
You have the belt.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.801
But this one's winner-take-all.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.100
-Yeah, this is
a unification right here.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.367
-You and Brock Lesnar,
who's not a small dude.

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.534
-No. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:01.734
I was trying to come up
with something.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.067
No, he's a --
-Yeah, no. He's --

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.067
-To be honest, he's a big boy.
-He's a big --

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.334
-He's a big ol' country boy.

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.767
-Yeah, he's giant,
and he scares me even just --

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.467
Even just saying his name
kind of scares me, too.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:11.801
-I got your back.
Don't worry.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:13.467
-Okay, good, thank you.
'Cause I was a little frightened

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.634
even just introducing you,
as well.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:22.601
This is you -- this is you in
"Wrestlemania 34" versus Brock.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:23.901
And this is just --

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:25.367
This is not --
We didn't color this.

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:27.501
-Oh, yeah.
-That is blood.

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:30.367
That is your blood on your --
on your face.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.200
-Yep, that's my blood.
Yep.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.000
-What's going through your --
-Brock did that, yep.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.033
-What's going through your mind
at this point?

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:41.067
-I think, in this moment,
I can finally see,

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.000
because once that blood
started coming down,

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.000
it gets in your eyeballs.
You know what I mean?

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.667
So --
For any of you who

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:50.634
have never had blood in your
eyeballs, it's quite thick.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.601
And it can completely blind you,
and you can't see.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:56.334
So I probably did one of these.
You know what I mean?

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:58.367
And then I saw it was Brock.
He's still there.

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:00.601
Aah!
-He didn't go away!

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:02.334
-Go away already!
-He didn't go away.

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.300
-He was still there.
-He was still there.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.234
That's even more frightening,
good.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:08.567
I appreciate the honesty.
-Yeah.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:11.901
-So, after this Saturday,
smoke clears, "Wrestlemania."

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:13.834
What are we gonna see?

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:15.534
-It's checkmate, man.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:18.767
It's time, you know, that we
close this chapter and move on.

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:22.234
You know, so, for me, I've been
on the run of a lifetime.

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:25.634
I think I've solidified myself
clearly in the modern day

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:28.534
as the greatest champion
to be a part of WWE.

00:07:28.534 --> 00:07:31.334
-That's right.
-And for me to kind of,

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:33.801
you know, get past this chapter
of Brock Lesnar,

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:37.067
I think it just puts me
on a playing field,

00:07:37.067 --> 00:07:40.167
on a level that no one else
can touch, so...

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.000
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.133
I have a feeling next time
you come on the show,

00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:46.133
you're gonna have
two championship belts.

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.734
Roman Reigns, everybody!

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:51.300
"Wrestlemania 38"
kicks off Saturday night.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.467
You can stream the two-day event
on Peacock.

